{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking","id":942357,"title":"Thought Experiment: Template Stacking","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-02T18:07:15-07:00","id":942357,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Thought Experiment: Template Stacking","content":"This got into my head and I've been struggling to get it out. And I don't have enough books / setting knowledge to just work through it to do so.<br /> <br /> So, for funsies:<br /> <br /> How many minor templates can you stack into a single character? How screwed is that person's life? And what, if any, major Template is best suited to the screwball situation that would allow that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1955-andoriol","name":"Andoriol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1955_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T18:37:04-07:00","id":942378,"title":"","content":"Deviant isn't even out yet, but I'm gonna say Deviant as the major template that would result. <br /> <br /> Also, this sounds like something a bunch of slightly drunk Cheiron scientists would dare each other to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T16:52:44-07:00","id":943109,"title":"","content":"Sam Haight already answered this question, and it turned him into an ashtray.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-03-2016, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:19:50-07:00","id":943271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking?p=943109#post943109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sam Haight already answered this question, and it turned him into an ashtray.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sam Haight is fun because he was so ridiculous and widely loathed that eventually he looped around to being hilarious, so much that I think most of the fans would love it if Onyx Path gave him a winking nod in a ChroD book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:37:25-07:00","id":943293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking?p=943271#post943271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sam Haight is fun because he was so ridiculous and widely loathed that eventually he looped around to being hilarious, so much that I think most of the fans would love it if Onyx Path gave him a winking nod in a ChroD book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I had a Geist campaign in which one of the players acquired an ashtray that occasionally screamed. He liked to hide it in people's houses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:43:16-07:00","id":943297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking?p=943271#post943271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sam Haight is fun because he was so ridiculous and widely loathed that eventually he looped around to being hilarious, so much that I think most of the fans would love it if Onyx Path gave him a winking nod in a ChroD book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, if you read the modules in which he appeared, people widely loathed him because they were a railroading mess of epic proportions, most of the time hinging on the ridiculous shit he'd pull out because of such template stacking, when in fact he was more often than not wearing better plot-armor than John Connor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:05:39-07:00","id":943324,"title":"","content":"I'm completely unfamiliar with Sam Haight, could someone cliff notes it for me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1955-andoriol","name":"Andoriol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1955_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:58:34-07:00","id":943364,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Samuel_Haight\" target=\"_blank\">He was an NPC who managed to stack templates for the big three in classic World of Darkness.</a><br /> <br /> Using second edition rules you could make a wolf-blooded ghoul, and I imagine you could make them a proximus too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-04-2016, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T21:58:53-07:00","id":943400,"title":"","content":"I think one of the most screwed up crossovers would be a Beloved Beholden Ghoul. On one hand, you have a Leviathan you're fanatically devoted to. On another, you're in need of a Mad Scientist to give you a world view. On a leg, you need a Vampire to feed you liquid love towards them. You're practically split between three people at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T05:20:55-07:00","id":943557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andoriol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking?p=943324#post943324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm completely unfamiliar with Sam Haight, could someone cliff notes it for me?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm going to use cofd terms since if you don't know about Haight you're probably not a big owod fan-<br /> <br /> Wolfblooded thaumaturge ghoul hunter who found a ritual that allowed him to become a werewolf after ritually murdering five werewolves, then became a mage by using a magic artifact to kill a thrysus archmaster, along the way effectively forming a new tribe of skindancer werewolves, and then made an artifact that stored his paradox so he could throw magic around willy nilly as much as he wants, had a fetish that gives him a spirit numina allowing him to teleport to safety whenever it was time to exit stage left, and died when he overloaded his paradox battery trying to get the blood of a BP 8 or 9 Belial's brood member, and only avoiding become a vampire werewolf because vampires warned him about the downsides of vampiredom, and that trying would most likely just kill him. <br /> <br /> So every time he showed up in a mage game, it's a safe bet the players wanted to kill him but weren't allowed to, every time he showed up in a werewolf game the players wanted to kill him but weren't allowed to, ironically, his interactions with vampires were supposed to be cordial- Instead of using his status as a werewolf mage to shake down vampires for blood, he'd just buy blood fair and square off vampires<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T06:46:44-07:00","id":943583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking?p=943364#post943364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Samuel_Haight\" target=\"_blank\">He was an NPC who managed to stack templates for the big three in classic World of Darkness.</a><br /> <br /> Using second edition rules you could make a wolf-blooded ghoul, and I imagine you could make them a proximus too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Offspring, too, probably. Fae-Touched probably wouldn't work, and there really isn't a minor splat worth mentioning in Promethean or Geist. I'm wondering how much they could keep if they were made Sadikh, too.<br /> <br /> Actually, wasn't there a Sam Haight in a slightly different name in Skinchangers?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T07:57:09-07:00","id":943622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking?p=943583#post943583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, wasn't there a Sam Haight in a slightly different name in Skinchangers?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Werewolf 20th Anniversary had a SAS called '<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/115057/Skinner-SAS\" target=\"_blank\">Skinner</a>,' which played upon Samuel Haight's legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T08:29:31-07:00","id":943646,"title":"","content":"So, of the major splats, you could theoretically have someone with (very limited) access to Disciplines, Tells, Arcana, and Embeds? Maybe Transmutations, if they go Alchemist?<br /> <br /> Any Blue Book stuff? I'd think Blood Bathing rituals would still work. Psychic powers and/or Thaumaturgy, probably. Skinchanging, maybe?<br /> <br /> I mean, the character would still have no Supernatural Tolerance (beyond that one merit in Hurt Locker), and their ability in those powers would likely suck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T08:47:19-07:00","id":943653,"title":"","content":"Ghouls have access to a lot of Disciplines. The only limitation would be clan disciplines, which would be limited to the regnant of the ghoul. I believe Changing Breeds had an ability to emulate mage spells, and that there's some way to copy Supernatural Tolerance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T09:24:36-07:00","id":943670,"title":"","content":"I'm unfamiliar with Changelings and Prometheans enough to guess at those, but STEAL ALL THE THINGS:<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf</b>:<br /> Mage - Eat a bloodline of Proximi and steal some of their blessings?<br /> <br /> Vampire - Could a Werewolf be made into a Ghoul? I would think that if they could, they'd be perfectly capable of maintaining being a Ghoul just by outright eating Vampires.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire:</b><br /> Mage - Feed off of enough of a kind of Proximi or functionally diablerize one. It'd probably require a Coil or something similar to allow the vampire to yoink Blessings or the ability to learn their own. Potentially originally requiring feeding off of a Mage of the appropriate Path and doing so relatively often to maintain it, but less so in progress through the Coil / whatever it is. <br /> <br /> Werewolf - Same concept as above, just eating Werewolves or Wolf Blooded.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage</b>:<br /> Vampire - ... could a mage be a Ghoul? If so, I'm not seeing any reason why they couldn't keep being one.<br /> <br /> Werewolf - This is the only one that feels weird and unlikely. A Shaman / dedicated Mage might be similar to a Wolf-Blooded or even a Werewolf in some ways, but I'm not seeing a way for the Mage to fully become a Wolf Blooded and gain access to Tells and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1955-andoriol","name":"Andoriol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1955_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T09:43:32-07:00","id":943680,"title":"","content":"Psychic powers wouldn't work with this and changing breeds are a full template which can only stack with wolf-blooded, alchemists and demon-blooded for sure (maybe fae-touched and proximi as well) so our hypothetical character loses out on 2 or 3 minor templates (ghoul, fae-touched and proximi potentially). Also ghouldom immediately forces you to sanctity all supernatural merits you previously possessed which means you have to choose between ghouldom and being a psychic, though if you count the hurt locker templates as separate you are better not taking ghouldom.<br /> <br /> I think the best you could stack (assuming you don't count the hurt locker templates as separate minor-templates to psychic) is:<br /> <br /> Ghoul (or psychic) / wolf-blooded / demon-blooded / alchemist / proximi / fae-touched<br /> <br /> So this would be a person who is born to a proximi dynasty (giving access to mage stuff through blessings), has their mother make a soul-pact with a demon and they become a demon-blooded out of the exchange (granting embeds), suffers a dramatic failure on a lunacy roll becoming a wolf-blooded (giving a wolf-blooded tell and the potential to gain renown / gifts through their pack and the potential for supernatural tolerance if they take the tell), are ghouled by a vampire (giving them disciplines), decide to go after prometheans and become an alchemist (giving them transmutations), have a friend they made a promise with become a changeling and they follow them into the hedge then become a fae-touched (gaining contracts). Which means we have a character who has renown, gifts, blessings, disciplines, contracts, transmutations, embeds and several kinds of supernatural tolerance, with no inbuilt weaknesses like fire or silver (even the 20 year life expectancy of fae-touched is overcome by being a ghoul). <br /> <br /> We could call her Samantha Haight, make her Samuel's cousin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T09:47:36-07:00","id":943684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andoriol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking?p=943670#post943670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unfamiliar with Changelings and Prometheans enough to guess at those, but STEAL ALL THE THINGS:<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf</b>:<br /> Mage - Eat a bloodline of Proximi and steal some of their blessings?<br /> <br /> Vampire - Could a Werewolf be made into a Ghoul? I would think that if they could, they'd be perfectly capable of maintaining being a Ghoul just by outright eating Vampires.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire:</b><br /> Mage - Feed off of enough of a kind of Proximi or functionally diablerize one. It'd probably require a Coil or something similar to allow the vampire to yoink Blessings or the ability to learn their own. Potentially originally requiring feeding off of a Mage of the appropriate Path and doing so relatively often to maintain it, but less so in progress through the Coil / whatever it is.<br /> <br /> Werewolf - Same concept as above, just eating Werewolves or Wolf Blooded.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage</b>:<br /> Vampire - ... could a mage be a Ghoul? If so, I'm not seeing any reason why they couldn't keep being one.<br /> <br /> Werewolf - This is the only one that feels weird and unlikely. A Shaman / dedicated Mage might be similar to a Wolf-Blooded or even a Werewolf in some ways, but I'm not seeing a way for the Mage to fully become a Wolf Blooded and gain access to Tells and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming we're running with actual rules legal things, so to address your points in turn<br /> <br /> Werewolves can't gain magic by eating the splats that possess the magic they want.<br /> <br /> Werewolves (and other full templates like mages) can't be ghouled<br /> <br /> Vampires can't diablerize anything but vampires, though we haven't had confirmation as to whether the proximi template stacks, so you could have a proximi that is turned into a vampire<br /> <br /> Vampires also can't gain powers of other splats by eating them<br /> <br /> Again, mages can't be ghouled<br /> <br /> And mages would have to have been wolf-blooded before their awakening in order to have a tell, no way to become one after they awaken","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T10:15:37-07:00","id":943692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking?p=943684#post943684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm assuming we're running with actual rules legal things, so to address your points in turn<br /> <br /> Werewolves can't gain magic by eating the splats that possess the magic they want.<br /> <br /> Werewolves (and other full templates like mages) can't be ghouled<br /> <br /> Vampires can't diablerize anything but vampires, though we haven't had confirmation as to whether the proximi template stacks, so you could have a proximi that is turned into a vampire<br /> <br /> Vampires also can't gain powers of other splats by eating them<br /> <br /> Again, mages can't be ghouled<br /> <br /> And mages would have to have been wolf-blooded before their awakening in order to have a tell, no way to become one after they awaken</div> </div> </div> </div>-blinks- Okay, I'm not <i>surprised </i>that full templates can't be ghouled, but I don't remember seeing that ever stated, and I'm surprised that I missed it. Do you remember roughly where it is so I can re-read and see what else I missed / totally forgot?<br /> <br /> And as for the EAT THINGS concepts, it'd likely require a specific subset of abilities to do so. Something like a specific &quot;Eat Things and Get Their Power&quot; Coil or such, as I <i>am </i>aware that they can't do that currently / RAW. I'd probably actually allow it as an ST, provided it <i>was </i>something like a Legacy or Coil and the character had to keep working at it in order to maintain the power (Like a Lich or Ghoul needing to get Souls / Vitae respectively), and then have the corresponding splat being fed upon react accordingly.<br /> <br /> And honestly at this point, I'd just wonder at ways to represent it mechanically that are remotely balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1955-andoriol","name":"Andoriol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1955_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T10:56:24-07:00","id":943716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking?p=943653#post943653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls have access to a lot of Disciplines. The only limitation would be clan disciplines, which would be limited to the regnant of the ghoul. I believe [REDACTED FROM MEMORY] had an ability to emulate mage spells, and that there's some way to copy Supernatural Tolerance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls havea very limited Vitae pool, and can't add Blood Potency to any rolls or effects, so there's that. Other than Proximi, the only way to copy mage spells is Forbidden Knowledge, I think. Or Demonic Show of Power chicanery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andoriol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking?p=943670#post943670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unfamiliar with Changelings and Prometheans enough to guess at those, but STEAL ALL THE THINGS:<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf</b>:<br /> Mage - Eat a bloodline of Proximi and steal some of their blessings?<br /> <br /> Vampire - Could a Werewolf be made into a Ghoul? I would think that if they could, they'd be perfectly capable of maintaining being a Ghoul just by outright eating Vampires.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire:</b><br /> Mage - Feed off of enough of a kind of Proximi or functionally diablerize one. It'd probably require a Coil or something similar to allow the vampire to yoink Blessings or the ability to learn their own. Potentially originally requiring feeding off of a Mage of the appropriate Path and doing so relatively often to maintain it, but less so in progress through the Coil / whatever it is.<br /> <br /> Werewolf - Same concept as above, just eating Werewolves or Wolf Blooded.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage</b>:<br /> Vampire - ... could a mage be a Ghoul? If so, I'm not seeing any reason why they couldn't keep being one.<br /> <br /> Werewolf - This is the only one that feels weird and unlikely. A Shaman / dedicated Mage might be similar to a Wolf-Blooded or even a Werewolf in some ways, but I'm not seeing a way for the Mage to fully become a Wolf Blooded and gain access to Tells and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much all of these are invalid. Major Templates cannot become Minor Templates (though Minor Templates can become <i>a</i> Major Template).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Or what has already been said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  Ninja'd... by waiting until after lunch. 08-04-2016, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T17:05:08-07:00","id":944009,"title":"","content":"Well... hmm. Do we want to consider Claimed as a (rather volatile) template too? It's technically a condition, sure, but it could potentially be played out at least vaguely like one, what with the new powers (Which according to the Promethean 2e entry on Claiming can be bought as merits), new needs (the Spooky Ephemeral Thingy may not bleed essence anymore but it's still gonna be hungry), new drawbacks (Bans! Banes! Being half-Spooky Ephemeral Thingy and obviously looking the part!), and being blatantly supernatural (what with being half-Spooky Ephemeral Thingy). And the Manifestation Effects table on page 131 of the ChroD core specifically calls out Supernatural Tolerance as one of the factors in the contesting roll, as does the table in the Created 2e core and the one in the Forsaken 2e core (the latter actually specifies Primal Urge). So it seems it can stack onto... well, anything that something else doesn't hold prior &quot;claim&quot; to, so long as the requirements have been met.<br /> <br /> Sooo... depending on what constitutes a &quot;template&quot; for the purpose of this thread, that could open up room for even more shenanigans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 08-04-2016, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T00:33:17-07:00","id":944178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andoriol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking?p=943692#post943692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-blinks- Okay, I'm not <i>surprised </i>that full templates can't be ghouled, but I don't remember seeing that ever stated, and I'm surprised that I missed it. Do you remember roughly where it is so I can re-read and see what else I missed / totally forgot?<br /> <br /> And as for the EAT THINGS concepts, it'd likely require a specific subset of abilities to do so. Something like a specific &quot;Eat Things and Get Their Power&quot; Coil or such, as I <i>am </i>aware that they can't do that currently / RAW. I'd probably actually allow it as an ST, provided it <i>was </i>something like a Legacy or Coil and the character had to keep working at it in order to maintain the power (Like a Lich or Ghoul needing to get Souls / Vitae respectively), and then have the corresponding splat being fed upon react accordingly.<br /> <br /> And honestly at this point, I'd just wonder at ways to represent it mechanically that are remotely balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Page 100 of VtR 2e core, the ghouls section says out that ghouls are mortals given kindred blood and a part of the vampire's power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T01:27:21-07:00","id":944187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking?p=944178#post944178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 100 of VtR 2e core, the ghouls section says out that ghouls are mortals given kindred blood and a part of the vampire's power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Represented by the willpower expenditure. A less taxing form of curse transference than say, the embrace which requires a whole dot instead of a point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T04:22:15-07:00","id":944236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking?p=944187#post944187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Represented by the willpower expenditure. A less taxing form of curse transference than say, the embrace which requires a whole dot instead of a point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I was glossing over that. My point was that ghouldom is something you can't give to anyone but a mortal (whether it be a human or animal).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T09:46:18-07:00","id":946237,"title":"","content":"This is such an astoundingly ridiculous idea that it rolls over to being brilliant. If you're ever running a more light-hearted horror-comedy chronicle, Samantha Haight would probably be a fantastic NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:03:41-07:00","id":946245,"title":"","content":"If you feel like including Homebrew methods, there is also Hedge Sorcerers and Affinity users.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:25:08-07:00","id":946264,"title":"","content":"A Vampire with the Coil of Zirnitra can stack as many off-template supernatural abilities as they please onto themselves, as long as they can find an appropriate body part.<br /> <br /> No one ever really <i>said</i> you can't have 13 arms and 5 heads, you know...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:22:20-07:00","id":946455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking?p=946264#post946264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Vampire with the Coil of Zirnitra can stack as many off-template supernatural abilities as they please onto themselves, as long as they can find an appropriate body part.<br /> <br /> No one ever really <i>said</i> you can't have 13 arms and 5 heads, you know...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's against one of the guidelines of social etiquette (Nth Edition). Mostly regarding the uncertainty of which head to talk to, I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:42:31-07:00","id":946469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking?p=946455#post946455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's against one of the guidelines of social etiquette (Nth Edition). Mostly regarding the uncertainty of which head to talk to, I believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>obviously the one with the hat relating to the topic in question, and failing that, the biggest one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T16:04:12-07:00","id":946528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942357-thought-experiment-template-stacking?p=946455#post946455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's against one of the guidelines of social etiquette (Nth Edition). Mostly regarding the uncertainty of which head to talk to, I believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>You label them, clearly.<br /> <br /> It's a miracle that anyone is able to get things done, having only one head to think, speak, and emote with. You'd think it would wear out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}